            }
          },
          "title": "the applied filter set",
          "type": "object"
        },
        "items": {
          "description": "The requested page, already windowed. Elements are item objects whose KEY SET depends on the request: the read tools compact by default (null and empty-list keys, plus the `schema` migration marker, are omitted — a missing `assignee` means unset, never unknown), `fields` projects to exactly the keys asked for, and `compact: false` restores every key. The full key set is item.json; no key is required here because any of them can be projected away.",
          "items": {
            "type": "object"
          },
          "type": "array"
        },
        "limit": {
          "description": "The page size in force, in the same encoding callers pass in: 0 means UNLIMITED, not \"empty page\". Echoed so a caller can read the effective cap rather than assume the MCP default (50).",
          "minimum": 0,
          "type": "integer"
        },
        "offset": {
          "description": "Rows skipped from the start of the ordered result.",
          "minimum": 0,
          "type": "integer"
        },
        "returned": {
          "description": "Elements in `items`.",
          "minimum": 0,
          "type": "integer"
        },
        "sort": {
          "description": "The ordering field in force. `relevance` is clove_search's default and cannot be requested on the other three.",
          "enum": [
            "rank",
            "priority",
            "created",
            "updated",
            "id",
            "status",
            "type",
            "relevance"
          ]
        },
        "source": {
          "description": "Which read tier answered: a running cloved, the SQLite index, or a file scan. The `_meta.source` of the CLI and web, carried as a plain key because this payload has no `_meta`.",
          "enum": [
            "daemon",
            "index",
            "files"
          ]
        },
        "total": {
          "description": "Matches BEFORE the window — always the full count, never the page size. `returned < total` means there is more to page through.",
          "minimum": 0,
          "type": "integer"
        }
      },
      "required": [
        "total",
        "returned",
        "offset",
        "limit",
        "sort",
        "dir",
        "items"
      ],
      "title": "clove MCP item page",
      "type": "object"
    }
  },
  {
    "description": "Create a new work item: one item per separate task, bug, or fix (the steps of one task are comments, not items). Give a `body` that stands on its own without this conversation: what is wrong or missing, where, and how to verify it is done. Returns its generated id and path.",
    "inputSchema": {
      "$schema": "https://json-schema.org/draft/2020-12/schema",
      "properties": {
        "assignee": {
          "description": "Assignee.",
          "type": [
            "string",
            "null"
          ]
        },
        "body": {
          "description": "Markdown body.",
          "type": [
            "string",
            "null"
          ]
        },
        "deps": {
          "description": "Ids this item hard-depends on.",
          "items": {
            "type": "string"
          },
          "type": [
            "array",
            "null"
          ]
        },
        "labels": {
          "description": "Labels to attach (case-insensitive).",
          "items": {
            "type": "string"
          },
          "type": [
            "array",
            "null"
          ]
        },
        "parent": {
          "description": "Parent item id (for epics).",
          "type": [
            "string",
            "null"
          ]
        },
        "priority": {
          "description": "Priority 0 (highest) .. 4 (default 2).",
          "format": "uint8",
          "maximum": 255,
          "minimum": 0,
          "type": [
            "integer",
            "null"
          ]
        },
        "title": {
          "description": "The item title (required).",
          "type": "string"
        },
        "type": {
          "description": "`bug|feature|chore|docs|epic`; defaults to the repo's configured type.",
          "type": [
            "string",
            "null"
          ]
        }
      },
      "required": [
        "title"
      ],
      "title": "NewArgs",
      "type": "object"
    },
    "name": "clove_new"
  },
  {
    "description": "List work items ready to start now: open/in-progress items whose hard dependencies are all closed and which have no dangling dependencies, ordered by (priority, topology). The primary 'what should I work on?' query.",
    "inputSchema": {
      "$defs": {
        "OneOrMany": {
          "anyOf": [
            {
              "type": "string"
            },
            {
              "items": {
                "type": "string"
              },
              "type": "array"
            }
          ],
          "description": "One value or a list of them.\n\nThe filter arguments accept `\"open\"` and `[\"open\",\"in_progress\"]` alike, so\nevery agent already calling these tools with a single string is unaffected —\nthe published `inputSchema` gains an `anyOf` branch rather than changing\ntype. `#[serde(untagged)]` is what makes the string form keep working; the\n`JsonSchema` derive mirrors it into the schema agents read."
        },
        "Priorities": {
          "anyOf": [
            {
              "format": "uint8",
              "maximum": 255,
              "minimum": 0,
              "type": "integer"
            },
            {
              "items": {
                "format": "uint8",
                "maximum": 255,
                "minimum": 0,
                "type": "integer"
              },
              "type": "array"
            }
          ],
          "description": "One priority or a list of them (`2` or `[0,1]`). Numeric, as it always was."
        }
      },
      "$schema": "https://json-schema.org/draft/2020-12/schema",
      "description": "Shared filter fields for `clove_ready` / `clove_list` / `clove_blocked`.",
      "properties": {
        "assignee": {
          "description": "Filter by assignee.",
          "type": [
            "string",
            "null"
          ]
        },
        "compact": {
          "description": "Omit null and empty-list keys. Defaults to true unless `fields` is given.",
          "type": [
            "boolean",
            "null"
          ]
        },
        "desc": {
          "description": "Reverse the sort order (newest-first, lowest-priority-first, ...).",
          "type": [
            "boolean",
            "null"
          ]
        },
        "fields": {
          "description": "Return only these keys per item (e.g. [\"id\",\"title\",\"status\"]). Unknown\nnames are ignored. Cuts list payloads by roughly two thirds.",
          "items": {
            "type": "string"
          },
          "type": [
            "array",
            "null"
          ]
        },
        "label": {
          "anyOf": [
            {
              "$ref": "#/$defs/OneOrMany"
            },
            {
              "type": "null"
            }
          ],
          "description": "Filter by label (case-insensitive). A list requires **all** of them."
        },
        "limit": {
          "description": "Max results (0 = no limit; default 50).",
          "format": "uint64",
          "minimum": 0,
          "type": [
            "integer",
            "null"
          ]
        },
        "offset": {
          "description": "Skip this many results.",
          "format": "uint64",
          "minimum": 0,
          "type": [
            "integer",
            "null"
          ]
        },
        "parent": {
          "description": "Only the direct children of this item id (e.g. `proj-7af3q2k9`).",
          "type": [
            "string",
            "null"
          ]
        },
        "priority": {
          "anyOf": [
            {
              "$ref": "#/$defs/Priorities"
            },
            {
              "type": "null"
            }
          ],
          "description": "Filter by priority (0=highest .. 4). A list matches any of them."
        },
        "q": {
          "description": "Keep only items whose id, title, or labels contain this text\n(case-insensitive). A filter, not a search: it never reads the body.",
          "type": [
            "string",
            "null"
          ]
        },
        "sort": {
          "description": "Sort by `rank|priority|created|updated|id|status|type`. Default `rank`:\npriority, then dependency order, then id.",
          "type": [
            "string",
            "null"
          ]
        },
        "status": {
          "anyOf": [
            {
              "$ref": "#/$defs/OneOrMany"
            },
            {
              "type": "null"
            }
          ],
          "description": "Filter by status (`open|in_progress|closed`). A list matches any of them."
        },
        "synced": {
          "description": "`true`: only items linked to an external tracker (any `external_ref`,\ne.g. a GitHub `gh-12`); `false`: only items with none.",
          "type": [
            "boolean",
            "null"
          ]
        },
        "type": {
          "anyOf": [
            {
              "$ref": "#/$defs/OneOrMany"
            },
            {
              "type": "null"
            }
          ],
          "description": "Filter by item type (`bug|feature|chore|docs|epic`). A list matches any\nof them."
        }
      },
      "title": "FilterArgs",
      "type": "object"
    },
    "name": "clove_ready",
    "outputSchema": {
      "$id": "https://clove.dev/schema/v1/mcp-item-page.json",
      "$schema": "https://json-schema.org/draft/2020-12/schema",
      "additionalProperties": false,
      "description": "The result of the MCP read tools that return a list: clove_list, clove_ready, clove_blocked, clove_search. This is the payload the server puts in `structuredContent` (and, byte-identically, in `content[0].text` for clients that do not read structured results), and it is what those tools advertise as their `outputSchema` in tools/list. It is the CLI's list envelope flattened: an MCP tool result has no `{v, ok, data, _meta}` wrapper, so the keys the CLI reports under `_meta` are plain keys beside `items` here.",
      "properties": {
        "dir": {
          "enum": [
            "asc",
            "desc"
          ]
        },
        "filters": {
          "additionalProperties": false,
          "description": "The parsed, canonicalized filters, echoed so a caller can read back what was applied rather than assume its input survived. Absent on clove_search, which takes no field filters — an empty object there would advertise a surface the tool does not have. Any-of within a field, all-of across fields; `labels` is all-of within the field too. An empty array does not constrain.",
          "properties": {
            "assignee": {
              "type": [
                "string",
                "null"
              ]
            },
            "labels": {
              "items": {
                "type": "string"
              },
              "type": "array"
            },
            "parent": {
              "description": "Only the direct children of this item id; null: no constraint.",
              "pattern": "^[a-z][a-z0-9]{0,7}-[0-9A-Z]{8}$",
              "type": [
                "string",
                "null"
              ]
            },
            "priority": {
              "items": {
                "maximum": 4,
                "minimum": 0,
                "type": "integer"
              },
              "type": "array"
            },
            "q": {
              "description": "Case-insensitive substring over id/title/labels (NOT bodies — that is clove_search).",
              "type": [
                "string",
                "null"
              ]
            },
            "status": {
              "items": {
                "enum": [
                  "open",
                  "in_progress",
                  "closed"
                ]
              },
              "type": "array"
            },
            "synced": {
              "description": "true: only items with a non-empty `external_ref` (any provider); false: only items without one; null: no constraint.",
              "type": [
                "boolean",
                "null"
              ]
            },
            "type": {
              "items": {
                "enum": [
                  "bug",
                  "feature",
                  "chore",
                  "docs",
                  "epic"
                ]
              },
              "type": "array"
            }
          },
          "title": "the applied filter set",
          "type": "object"
        },
        "items": {
          "description": "The requested page, already windowed. Elements are item objects whose KEY SET depends on the request: the read tools compact by default (null and empty-list keys, plus the `schema` migration marker, are omitted — a missing `assignee` means unset, never unknown), `fields` projects to exactly the keys asked for, and `compact: false` restores every key. The full key set is item.json; no key is required here because any of them can be projected away.",
          "items": {
            "type": "object"
          },
          "type": "array"
        },
        "limit": {
          "description": "The page size in force, in the same encoding callers pass in: 0 means UNLIMITED, not \"empty page\". Echoed so a caller can read the effective cap rather than assume the MCP default (50).",
          "minimum": 0,
          "type": "integer"
        },
        "offset": {
          "description": "Rows skipped from the start of the ordered result.",
          "minimum": 0,
          "type": "integer"
        },
        "returned": {
          "description": "Elements in `items`.",
          "minimum": 0,
          "type": "integer"
        },
        "sort": {
          "description": "The ordering field in force. `relevance` is clove_search's default and cannot be requested on the other three.",
          "enum": [
            "rank",
            "priority",
            "created",
            "updated",
            "id",
            "status",
            "type",
            "relevance"
          ]
        },
        "source": {
          "description": "Which read tier answered: a running cloved, the SQLite index, or a file scan. The `_meta.source` of the CLI and web, carried as a plain key because this payload has no `_meta`.",
          "enum": [
            "daemon",
            "index",
            "files"
          ]
        },
        "total": {
          "description": "Matches BEFORE the window — always the full count, never the page size. `returned < total` means there is more to page through.",
          "minimum": 0,
          "type": "integer"
        }
      },
      "required": [
        "total",
        "returned",
        "offset",
        "limit",
        "sort",
        "dir",
        "items"
      ],
      "title": "clove MCP item page",
      "type": "object"
    }
  },
  {
    "description": "Search item titles, labels, and bodies for a case-insensitive SUBSTRING (not whole words: `core` matches `corepart`). Title matches rank first, then labels, then bodies.",
    "inputSchema": {
      "$schema": "https://json-schema.org/draft/2020-12/schema",
